menu "esp-otp hardware"

    config OTP_I2C_SDA_GPIO
        int "I2C SDA GPIO (OLED + optional DS3231)"
        default 5
        help
            Shared I2C data line. Avoid strapping pins (2, 8, 9).

    config OTP_I2C_SCL_GPIO
        int "I2C SCL GPIO (OLED + optional DS3231)"
        default 6

    config OTP_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "Push button GPIO (active low)"
        default 9
        help
            The C3 super mini's onboard BOOT button is on GPIO9 (active low,
            has a pull-up). Reused here as the user button. Don't hold it at
            power-on or the ROM enters USB download mode.

    config OTP_DEMO_MODE
        bool "Demo mode (seed a test secret + time at boot)"
        default n
        help
            For QEMU/bring-up: if the store is empty, seed a demo TOTP secret,
            and if time is unset, set a fixed epoch so a code is computed
            immediately without a host. Leave OFF for production.

endmenu
